# dashboard-linter configuration for dashboards generated by dashboard-architect.
#
# The linter defaults target single-binary Prometheus exporters, where `job` and
# `instance` identify a scrape target. Dashboards built by this skill scope by
# Kubernetes topology instead, so the four job/instance rules are excluded and
# replaced by the cluster/namespace/pod convention in references/conventions.md.
#
# Everything else stays an error on purpose: those rules enforce conventions the
# skill states but cannot check on its own.

exclusions:
  template-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      Dashboards scope by cluster, namespace, and pod rather than by scrape job.
      The job label is used to discover related metrics, not to filter panels.
  template-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      Pod identity replaces instance identity on Kubernetes, where instance is a
      churning pod IP rather than a stable host.
  target-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      See template-job-rule. Queries carry cluster and namespace matchers instead.
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      See template-instance-rule. Queries carry pod or node matchers instead.
  uneditable-dashboard:
    reason: >-
      Generated dashboards stay editable so a user can adjust them in place. The
      ai-generated tag records provenance instead of a read-only flag.
